# Docker build context.
#
# Without this, `docker build` uploads the entire working tree — including
# ~840 MB of node_modules and every Chromium download — to the daemon before it
# runs a single instruction. The Dockerfiles install their own dependencies from
# the lockfile, so none of it is wanted.

# Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build output: rebuilt inside the image. Copying a host build in would also
# risk shipping artefacts compiled against a different libc.
dist/
**/dist/
.next/
**/.next/
out/
**/out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Caches
.turbo/
.cache/
**/.cache/
coverage/

# Local runtime state
var/
storage/
tmp/
*.log

# Secrets. The example file is kept because it documents the configuration
# surface; the real one must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Infrastructure that is applied, not built into an image
infra/tofu/
infra/helm/
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Docs and integrations. The API and web images need neither; the Moodle plugin
# and the n8n node are published separately.
docs/
integrations/
*.md
!README.md

# The generated template library IS needed — the API serves it — so it is
# deliberately not excluded here.
